# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output. `dist-host/` is the Host build (ADR 0013) — a second artifact of the same
# source, produced by `pnpm --filter @wynding/web build:host` and packaged by the native
# hosts. Ignored for the same reason `dist/` is: it is generated on every build.
dist/
dist-perf/
dist-host/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tooling caches
.turbo/
coverage/
*.log

# Playwright run artifacts
test-results/
**/test-results/

# Env
.env
.env.local

# iOS signing identity (#135). A development team ID is a durable, personally-linked
# identifier and this repository is PUBLIC, so it never enters a tracked file. The developer
# writes DEVELOPMENT_TEAM here; `ios/debug.xcconfig` and `ios/release.xcconfig` each pull it
# in with an OPTIONAL include, so a clone without this file still builds. Never remove this
# rule to "fix" a signing problem — see apps/mobile/README.md for the intended workflow.
apps/mobile/ios/LocalSigning.xcconfig

# Reference material from inspiring games — competitive research lives here and
# stays OUT of the tracked repo (clean-room boundary).
research/

# AI agent tooling — installed locally, not committed (see docs/ai-workflow.md)
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*

# Working artifacts of the grill-with-docs-codex loop. PLAN.md is a scratch plan for one
# task and PLAN-REVIEW-LOG.md is its argument transcript with Codex — both are session
# state, superseded the moment the work lands. What survives goes to an ADR, a design
# note, or the issue. CONTEXT.md is deliberately NOT here: the glossary is tracked.
#
# ANCHORED to the repo root, because these are created at the root and nowhere else. Without
# the leading slash git matches every path component at every depth, so a deliberately-tracked
# `apps/mobile/PLAN.md` — and ADR 0012 expects both native projects to arrive under #135 —
# would vanish silently.
#
# Stated precisely, since the anchoring cuts both ways: this rule is NARROWER than the
# unanchored pair in a local `.git/info/exclude`, so a scratch file written under a
# subdirectory is neither tracked nor ignored and `git add -A` would sweep it into a commit.
# That is the accepted trade — a silently-vanished source file is worse than a visibly-added
# scratch one — and the obligation it leaves is simply: keep these two at the root.
/PLAN.md
/PLAN-REVIEW-LOG.md
